The Biggest Question :
If Hardware Exists, Why Can't Applications Directly Use It?
___________________________________________________________

For example:
Why can't Chrome directly talk to:

CPU
RAM
SSD
Keyboard

without an OS?
Imagine No Operating System

You open:
Chrome
VS Code
Spotify
WhatsApp

All applications want:
CPU time
RAM
Disk access
at the same time.

Who will decide?
Nobody.
Chaos.

Example: One Bathroom, Four People
Suppose there is:
1 bathroom
4 people
Without management:
Everyone rushes inside.
Result:
Fight.

Computer has similar problem:
1 CPU
Many programs
OS decides:

Chrome -> Wait
VS Code -> Run
Spotify -> Wait

This is called:
CPU Scheduling
______________

# Problem 2: RAM Conflict
_________________________

Suppose:
Chrome stores data at RAM location:
1000
Now Spotify also writes:
1000
Data gets overwritten.
Crash.
OS prevents this.

Example:
Chrome -> RAM 1000-5000
Spotify -> RAM 5001-9000
This is:
Memory Management
__________________

Problem 3: File Corruption
___________________________
Imagine two apps writing to the same file.

Without OS:
App A writes
App B writes
App A writes
App B writes
File becomes corrupted.
OS coordinates access.
This is:
File Management

Security Disaster
Suppose a calculator app decides:
Let me delete all photos.
Without OS:
Nothing stops it.
OS creates permissions.

Examples:
Read
Write
Execute
This is:
Protection & Security
